course: dictionary
lesson: 7181
title: Personality and context
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. In «Each ghost in Pac-Man had its own simple rules, which made them feel like different personalities», personality means the character or way of behaving that each ghost seems to have.
explain: Personality can also mean a lively, interesting character. Look at the words around it. In «She has lots of personality», the words lots of tell you the meaning is about how much character someone has, and it is praise.
explain: Context can also hide a meaning. «He has a nice personality» sounds kind, but it is often a sly way to say someone is not good-looking. When praise sounds too small or strange, think about what the speaker really means.
fact: Your personality is the kind of person you are: your character, the way you think, feel and behave.
fact: A personality can be a famous person, especially on TV, radio or in sport, as in «a TV personality».
fact: Writers show a character's personality through what the character says and does.
fact: «Strong personality» on a school report often means bossy or defiant, so check the other words on the report for clues.
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Her personality shines when she tells jokes.» What does personality mean here? | *The kind of person she is | The name on her school bag | A famous TV star | A loud noise
exercise: «She has lots of personality.» What does this suggest about her? | She is very tall | *She is lively and interesting | She is lost | She is asleep
exercise: Which of these is a TV personality? | *A presenter who hosts a popular TV quiz | A cloud over the sea | A dog that sleeps all day | A tap in the kitchen
test: «He has a nice personality.» Why might this be a sly compliment? | *Because it can mean he is not good-looking | Because it means he is very tall | Because it is the first sentence in a story | Because it is a sentence about a famous TV star
test: Which of these describes a personality trait? | Cat, dog or horse | Red, round or heavy | Monday, Tuesday or Friday | *Shy, brave or bossy
exam: «Strong personality» on a school report often means what? | Very quiet and shy | *Bossy or defiant | Very tall and strong | Good at maths
